---
import { url, NEWSLETTER } from '../config';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Bridge from '../components/Bridge.astro';

import NewsletterForm from '../components/NewsletterForm.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Base title="Unlock the Week: a one-minute tech fix every Wednesday" description="Unlock the Week by NeonKey: one short email every Wednesday with a one-minute fix for your tech or your customer follow-up, plus a free guide from Learn. For small businesses, people starting one, and anyone who wants their tech to behave.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Newsletter · Every Wednesday" title="Unlock the Week" crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { label: 'Newsletter' }]} class="nl-head">
    <p class="lede">One short email every Wednesday with one fix you can do in a few minutes: keep your tech secure, or catch more of the customers who reach out. Plus a free guide from Learn. Written with small businesses in mind, and useful whether you run one, are starting one, or just want your own tech to behave.</p>
    <Fragment slot="meta">
      <li><span>Every Wednesday</span></li>
      <li><span>About a one-minute read</span></li>
      <li><span>Free</span></li>
      <li><span>One-click unsubscribe</span></li>
    </Fragment>
    <div class="nl-box topline nl-subscribe" slot="after">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem">Subscribe</h2>
      <NewsletterForm id="page-nl" />
      <p class="form-note" style="margin-top:.6rem">After you confirm, reply "yes" to the welcome email and we'll send the One-Minute Fix List: 12 fixes on one page.</p>
    </div>
  </PageHeader>
  <section style="padding-top:1rem" aria-labelledby="get-h">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeading id="get-h" eyebrow="Inside every issue" title="What you get" />
      <div class="grid grid-2 nl-get">
        <div class="card topline accent-cyan"><div class="panel-head"><span class="icon-chip"><Icon name="shield" /></span><h3>Tech tips that keep you secure</h3></div><p>Small, practical fixes for the accounts, email, backups and Wi-Fi your business runs on, explained step by step without jargon. Most work just as well at home.</p></div>
        <div class="card topline accent-magenta"><div class="panel-head"><span class="icon-chip"><Icon name="spark" /></span><h3>Catch more customers</h3></div><p>Simple habits for the inquiries you already get: faster replies, missed calls, quotes that went quiet and reviews. No ads to buy, no new software required.</p></div>
        <div class="card topline accent-violet"><div class="panel-head"><span class="icon-chip"><Icon name="wrench" /></span><h3>A free guide from Learn</h3></div><p>When it fits the topic, each issue points to a free guide in <a href={url('/learn/')}>Learn</a> so you can go deeper at your own pace.</p></div>
        <div class="card topline accent-amber"><div class="panel-head"><span class="icon-chip"><Icon name="clock" /></span><h3>Short, and easy to leave</h3></div><p>One email a week, readable in about a minute. Your email is used only to send the newsletter and is never sold. Signups are handled by Kit; see the <a href={url('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt" aria-labelledby="who-h">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeading id="who-h" eyebrow="Who it's for" title="One fix a week, whoever you are" />
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card"><h3>Small business owners and office managers</h3><p>You run the shop, answer the phone and keep the computers working. Each issue is one thing you can fix between jobs, often before lunch.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>People starting something</h3><p>Setting up a new business, side project or freelance gig? Get the basics right from day one: a secure email, a contact form that works, backups and a simple way to follow up.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Anyone who wants their tech to behave</h3><p>Two-step login, backups, scam emails and Wi-Fi work the same at home. If you're here for the tips and Learn guides, you're in the right place.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="format-h">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeading id="format-h" eyebrow="Issue format" title="What an issue looks like" />
      <article class="card issue-format topline">
        <header class="issue-masthead">
          <span class="issue-brand">Unlock the Week</span>
          <span class="kicker">Issue format</span>
        </header>
        <h3>Unlock the Week #2: Fill out your own contact form tonight</h3>
        <ol class="step-cards issue-sections">
          <li><strong>One line up top:</strong> the idea in a sentence, like "The fastest reply usually wins the job."</li>
          <li><strong>This week's one-minute fix:</strong> one problem, why it matters, and the exact steps. Under 200 words.</li>
          <li><strong>One link:</strong> a Lab demo, a service or a guide that fits the fix.</li>
          <li><strong>From Learn:</strong> a free guide when it fits.</li>
          <li><strong>P.S.:</strong> a question for you. Hit reply anytime; every reply gets read.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:.6rem 0 0;font-size:.92rem">Coming up: missed calls, quotes that went quiet, emails landing in spam, holiday payment scams, backups and a ten-minute Wi-Fi checkup.{NEWSLETTER.mode === 'off' ? ' Signups open soon.' : ''}</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Bridge location="newsletter" text="Every issue connects to the rest of NeonKey: a free Learn guide, a Lab demo you can try, and the services behind them." links={[{ href: '/learn/', label: 'Browse Learn' }, { href: '/lab/', label: 'Try a Lab demo', event: 'lab-cta' }, { href: '/free-it-kit/', label: 'Get the free IT kit' }]} />
  <!-- Meta and Reddit pixels (PageView) for the newsletter ad test. -->
  <script is:inline src={url('/js/ad-pixels.js')}></script>
</Base>
